quinn-udp: IP_RECVTOS on QNX.

quinn-udp requests IP_RECVTOS (for ECN) on every system but OpenBSD, NetBSD
and Solaris, reading it from the libc crate. QNX has the option -- 68, as on
FreeBSD, in <netinet/in.h> -- but libc does not export it for
target_os = "nto" ("cannot find value IP_RECVTOS in crate libc"). Define it
locally on QNX.

Applied to quinn-udp 0.5.5 (the version zenoh-c's Cargo.lock pins) by
ports/zenoh-c/recipe.sh.

Upstream-Status: Pending (the constant belongs in the libc crate)

--- a/src/unix.rs
+++ b/src/unix.rs
@@ -24,6 +24,13 @@
     IO_ERROR_LOG_INTERVAL,
 };
 
+// QNX defines IP_RECVTOS (68, as FreeBSD does) in <netinet/in.h>, but the libc
+// crate does not export it for target_os = "nto".
+#[cfg(target_os = "nto")]
+const IP_RECVTOS: libc::c_int = 68;
+#[cfg(not(target_os = "nto"))]
+use libc::IP_RECVTOS;
+
 // Defined in netinet6/in6.h on OpenBSD, this is not yet exported by the libc crate
 // directly.  See https://github.com/rust-lang/libc/issues/3704 for when we might be able to
 // rely on this from the libc crate.
